00:15:46,257 --> 00:15:50,477
로컬 GPU가 있었는데 긴 RL
실험을 돌리고 싶었거든요.

262
00:15:50,477 --> 00:15:53,107
그리고 보통 집을 비울
땐 콘센트를 다 뽑아두는
And usually I also unplug things because you never know if you're not at home, you don't want things plugged in.

263
00:15:53,107 --> 00:15:56,141
편이에요, 집에 없을 때 뭐가
꽂혀 있으면 모르니까요.

264
00:15:56,141 --> 00:15:57,941
근데 실수로 GPU를 뽑아버린 거예요.
And I accidentally unplugged the GPU.

265
00:15:57,941 --> 00:16:01,580
아내는 이미 차에 타 있었는데,
'아, 이런' 싶더라고요.
My wife was already in the car and it's like, "Oh dang."

266
00:16:01,580 --> 00:16:05,189
그래서 제 여러 실험이랑 평가를 돌리는
Then basically I wanted as fast as possible a Bash script that runs my different experiments and the evaluation.

267
00:16:05,189 --> 00:16:09,313
Bash 스크립트가
최대한 빨리 필요했어요.

268
00:16:09,313 --> 00:16:13,009
Bash 인터페이스나 터미널
쓰는 법이야 알긴 아는데,
And it's something I know, I learned how to use the Bash interface or Bash terminal, but in that moment I just needed like 10 seconds, give me the command. - This is a hilarious situation but yeah, so what did you use? - So I did the non-thinking fastest model.

269
00:16:13,009 --> 00:16:16,829
그 순간엔 그냥 10초 안에
명령어만 딱 주면 됐거든요.

270
00:16:16,829 --> 00:16:20,279
— 진짜 웃긴 상황인데요,
그래서 뭘 쓰셨어요? —

271
00:16:20,279 --> 00:16:24,098
그때는 가장 빠른
non-thinking 모델을 썼어요.

272
00:16:24,098 --> 00:16:28,871
그게 여러 스크립트를 이어붙이는
Bash 명령어를 줬는데,
It gave me the Bash command to chain different scripts to each other and then the thing is like you have the tee thing where you want to route this to a log file.

273
00:16:28,871 --> 00:16:33,942
그 안에 로그 파일로 보내는
tee 같은 것도 들어 있었어요.

274
00:16:33,942 --> 00:16:36,998
머리로 생각하면 저도 알아낼 수
있었겠지만, 그때는 그냥 급했어요.
Top of my head I was just like in a hurry, I could have thought about it myself. - By the way I don't know if there's a representative case, wife waiting in the car- ... you have to run, you know, unplug the GPU.

275
00:16:36,998 --> 00:16:39,641
— 그나저나 이게 대표적인
사례인지는 모르겠는데요, 아내는

276
00:16:39,641 --> 00:16:42,449
차에서 기다리고 있죠, 뛰어가야
하고, GPU도 뽑아놨고...

277
00:16:42,449 --> 00:16:43,931
Bash 스크립트도 만들어야 하고요.
You have to generate a Bash script.

278
00:16:43,931 --> 00:16:45,977
완전 영화 같네요, 무슨
미션 임파서블처럼요.
This sounds like a movie, like- Mission Impossible. - I use Gemini for that.

279
00:16:45,977 --> 00:16:47,777
— 그럴 때는 제가 Gemini를 써요.

280
00:16:47,777 --> 00:16:51,669
그래서 정보 찾는 일에는
thinking을 쓰고, 빠르게 처리할
So I use thinking for all the information stuff and then Gemini for fast things or stuff that I could sometimes Google, which is like it's good at explaining things and I trust that it has this kind of background of knowledge and it's simple.

281
00:16:51,669 --> 00:16:55,561
일이나 가끔 구글링해도 될 만한
건 Gemini를 써요. 설명을

282
00:16:55,561 --> 00:16:59,231
잘해주고, 배경지식도 탄탄하다는
믿음이 있고, 간단하거든요.

283
00:16:59,231 --> 00:17:02,983
그리고 Gemini 앱도 많이
좋아졌고요— 그런 일엔 딱이에요.
And the Gemini app has gotten a lot better and- It's good for those sorts of things.

284
00:17:02,983 --> 00:17:05,263
그리고 코드나 철학적인 대화 같은 건
And then for code and any sort of philosophical discussion, I use Claude Opus 4.5.

285
00:17:05,263 --> 00:17:07,543
Claude Opus 4.5를 써요.

286
00:17:07,543 --> 00:17:09,555
이것도 항상 extended
thinking으로요.
Also always with extended thinking.

287
00:17:09,555 --> 00:17:12,445
extended thinking이랑
인퍼런스 스케일링은 그냥
Extended thinking and inference time scaling is just a way to make the models marginally smarter.

288
00:17:12,445 --> 00:17:15,073
모델을 아주 조금 더 똑똑하게
만드는 방법일 뿐이에요.

289
00:17:15,073 --> 00:17:17,964
그리고 발전 속도가 이렇게
빠를 땐 저는 항상 그쪽으로
And I will always err on that side when the progress is very high because you don't know when that'll unlock a new use case.

290
00:17:17,964 --> 00:17:21,241
기우는 편이에요, 언제 새로운
활용 사례가 열릴지 모르니까요.

291
00:17:21,241 --> 00:17:26,192
그리고 실시간 정보나, 분명 봤던 건
기억나는데 다시 찾아야 하고 거기에
And then sometimes use Grok for real-time information or finding something on AI Twitter that I knew I saw and I need to dig up and I just fixated on.

292
00:17:26,192 --> 00:17:30,772
꽂혀버린 AI 트위터 글 같은 걸
파낼 때는 가끔 Grok을 써요.

293
00:17:30,772 --> 00:17:34,116
근데 Grok 4가 나왔을
때, 그러니까 프로 버전격인
Although when Grok 4 came out, the Grok 4 SuperGrok Heavy, which was like their pro variant was actually very good and I was pretty impressed with it, and then it just kind of like muscle memory lost track of it with having the ChatGPT app open.

294
00:17:34,116 --> 00:17:37,572
Grok 4 SuperGrok
Heavy가 진짜 괜찮았고

295
00:17:37,572 --> 00:17:40,581
저도 꽤 인상 깊었는데,
그러다가 그냥 습관적으로

296
